From 5bf56277f540f58f0a30dc606261efb19fbee917 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Deng, Bing" <bing.deng@intel.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 09:15:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Fix crash/race risks and an info-leak in the ROS2 node

Major bug fixes:
1. Wrap main() in a try/catch so a startup exception logs a clear
   fatal message through RCLCPP_FATAL instead of taking down the
   node with an unhandled exception.
2. Reorder a few null-pointer checks so the pointer is tested
   before it gets dereferenced, add an explicit lidar pointer
   guard in ImuProcess::Process2 next to the existing assert, and
   move the mutex lock in imu_prop_callback and img_cbk so the
   shared state they read is actually covered by the lock instead
   of being checked just before it.
3. Guard against division by zero in three VIO score/residual
   computations, free the scratch patch buffer in
   updateVisualMapPoints when a point ends up not being added, and
   reject the degenerate zero-area case in plane_judge before it
   divides by the cross-product magnitude.
4. Trim an internal IP address from the camera intrinsics config
   comment, which a BDBA scan flagged as an information-leakage
   finding, keeping the capture date and camera serial number for
   traceability; add a maintainer entry in package.xml.

Signed-off-by: Deng, Bing <bing.deng@intel.com>
